@startuml sequence_experiment_submit
!theme plain
title Experiment Submit – Setup -> Queue

actor User
participant "Setup Page\n(Streamlit)" as Setup
participant "api_client\n(httpx)" as Client
participant "FastAPI\n/app.py" as API
participant "db.py\n(SQLite WAL)" as DB
participant "Dispatcher\n(asyncio loop)" as Disp
participant "Runner\n(subprocess)" as Runner
participant "Trainer\n(baselines)" as Trainer

== Form fill & validate ==
User -> Setup: fill tabs (env, algos, params, budget, ...)
Setup -> Setup: coerce values\n(bound checks, type casts)
User -> Setup: click "Validate"
Setup -> Client: POST /experiments/validate\n{ExperimentSpec}
Client -> API: HTTP POST
API -> API: validate_spec(spec)\n(table-driven: env, algo, params, budget, ...)
API --> Client: 200 {ok, errors[], warnings[]}
Client --> Setup: ValidationReport
Setup --> User: render errors/warnings by tab

== Submit ==
User -> Setup: click "Submit"
Setup -> Client: POST /experiments\n{ExperimentSpec}
Client -> API: HTTP POST
API -> API: validate_spec(spec) (defense in depth)
note right of API: 422 if invalid
API -> DB: insert_experiment(spec, status="queued")
DB --> API: experiment_id
API --> Client: 201 {id, status="queued", position}
Client --> Setup: SubmitResponse
Setup --> User: success toast + navigate to Queue

== Submit (custom script — Setup → Advanced) ==
note over Setup, API: gated by DEAP_ENABLE_ADVANCED (else 403)
User -> Setup: Advanced tab → paste script → "Submit to queue"
Setup -> Client: POST /experiments/script {script, label}
Client -> API: HTTP POST
API -> API: validate_script_source(script)\n(ast.parse + structural checks)
note right of API: 422 {ok:false, issues} if syntax error
API -> DB: insert_experiment(\n  {kind:"script", environment:"(custom script)", script}, queued)
DB --> API: experiment_id
API --> Client: 201 {id, status="queued", position}

== Dispatch ==
Disp -> Disp: _loop: poll every 1s
Disp -> DB: dequeue_next()\n(min enqueue_seq, not paused)
DB --> Disp: experiment (spec_json, id)
Disp -> Disp: parse spec_json → kind ("spec" | "script")
Disp -> DB: set_running(id)
Disp -> Disp: open _stdout.log

alt kind == "script"
    Disp -> Disp: write user_script.py
    Disp -> Runner: Popen([python, user_script.py],\n  cwd=<experiment-dir>, env=PYTHONPATH+=DEAP_PROJECT_ROOT,\n  stdout=_stdout.log)
else kind == "spec" (default)
    Disp -> Runner: Popen([python, -m, deap_pettingzoo.service.runner,\n  --spec-file <path>, --experiment-dir <dir>],\n  stdout=_stdout.log)
end
note right of Disp: logger.info "Experiment {id} running (pid, log)"\n(diagnostic log — see sequence_logging_pipeline.puml)

== Training ==
Runner -> Runner: configure_logging()\n(console only; level inherited via DEAP_LOG_LEVEL env)
Runner -> Runner: load spec → re-validate
Runner -> Runner: build_configs(spec) → [SubRun, ...]
note right of Runner: logger.info component activation\n(env, algorithms, budget, parallelism, coevolution)
loop for each SubRun (algo × seed)
    Runner -> Runner: print + logger.info "Starting [i/N] {algo} seed"
    Runner -> Trainer: trainer.train(config, progress_callback=writer.cb)
    activate Trainer
    Trainer -> Runner: progress_callback(ProgressEvent)
    Runner -> Runner: atomic write _progress.json\n(tmp + os.replace)
    deactivate Trainer
end
note right of Runner: on failure: logger.exception(...) before _result.json
Runner -> Runner: write _result.json\n{status, run_dirs[], error?}
Runner --> Disp: exit 0 (success) or 1 (failure)

== Completion ==
Disp -> Runner: await proc.wait()
note right of Disp: kind=="script": synthesise _result.json from exit code\n+ run_dirs discovered via rglob("manifest.json")
Disp -> Disp: read _result.json
Disp -> DB: exit=0 → set_completed\n≠0 → set_failed
note right of Disp: completed → logger.info\nfailed → logger.error "Experiment {id} failed: ..."
Disp --> DB: done

@enduml
